      "writtenOn": "2018-04-03T14:04:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hm, if I\u0027m not mistaken these always go in pairs? Have you considered including struct leaf_data_t in imported_leaf_data_t? Or alternatively, would it make sense to just add pointers in imported_leaf_data_t backed by pub and cipher_text buffers in unimported_leaf_data_t? For pub that should be trivial, for cipher_text it depends on whether we can encrypt/decrypt in-place. Can we? The DCRYPTO code suggests so, but I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s OK to rely on that. Even if not, we could declare an inline leaf_sensitive_data_t field in imporated_leaf_data_t that receives the decrypted data?\n\nThe reason I\u0027m asking is because I\u0027m hoping we could drop the additional layer of struct/buffers represented by struct leaf_data_t. WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 425,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 426,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "7b834d2fd6e6054282a20a87ea450d338bbad44d",
